 (Lane H) — complete\n\nExactly one new file was created, as the packet mandates: `AristotleCandidates/LocalHyperbolicAlgebraicAlpha.lean` (1025 lines). `lake build AristotleCandidates.LocalHyperbolicAlgebraicAlpha` succeeds with **no errors and no warnings**; the file contains no `sorry`, `admit`, `axiom`, `opaque`, `unsafe` or `implemented_by`, and `#print axioms` on the main results reports only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound`.\n\n### Answer to the packet's reporting question\n\n**No stage equivalence remains supplied.** Every finite-stage star equivalence, every connecting map, and the global `alpha` is *constructed* from the P52 coordinate data; the structure `AlphaData` contains no `StarAlgEquiv`, no algebra, and no coherence hypothesis as a field.\n\n### 1. Checked infrastructure developed in the packet\n\n* A concrete **twisted Pauli word algebra** `pauliAlgebra B` for any finite F₂-label group with an F₂-bilinear pairing `B` (`PauliForm`): a star-subalgebra of a complex matrix algebra. Proved: the multiplier law `word v · word w = (-1)^{B v w} • word (v+w)`, the involution law `star (word v) = (-1)^{B v v} • word v`, linear independence of the words, hence a complex **word basis** `pauliWordBasis`, and the induced `twistHom` star-algebra map of a form-preserving label map together with its uniqueness.\n* The **global coordinate pairing** `coordPairing`, its restriction to the stage label modules, and the key lemma relating the ZMod-4 coordinate bilinear form to a `PauliForm`.\n* The **finite stages**: source labels `sourceLabels n ⊆ (I ⊕ I) →₀ F₂` and target labels `targetLabels n ⊆ (L ⊕ L) →₀ F₂` from P52, their finiteness, the stage label map, its **bijectivity**, and the adapted Z/X coordinate basis of each stage.\n* The **phase calibration**: the explicit ZMod-4 quadratic refinement `qGlobal` of the coordinate discrepancy of the two Pauli cocycles, with proofs of the exact multiplier equation and the exact involution equation at every stage.\n* The **connecting maps** on both sides, their `DirectedSystem` instances, the assembled P29 stage data and the P30 `DirectedFiniteCoordinateFamily` (its four compatibility fields proved, not assumed).\n\n### 2. Theorem recovered in the manuscript's intended form\n\n* `AlphaData.alpha` — the coherent algebraic direct-limit `StarAlgEquiv` between the algebraic limit of the finite Pauli algebras and the algebraic limit of the finite regional algebras.\n* `alpha_word` — the Pauli-word formula at every stage; `alpha_symm_word` — the inverse formula.\n* `alpha_zWord` / `alpha_xWord` — the manuscript's `α(Z_i) = P(z_i)` and `α(X_i) = P(x_i)` (source basis `main.tex:1898-1944`), in phase-calibrated form: the image is the regional Pauli word of `z i` (resp. `x i`) times the explicit calibration phase, which `phase_ne_zero` shows is a fourth root of unity.\n* `existsUnique_alpha` — `alpha` is the unique star-algebra equivalence of the two algebraic limits obeying the stagewise phase-calibrated word formula.\n\n### 3. Conditional content: the exact extra assumptions\n\nBeyond the integrated P52 data (`LocalHyperbolicFamily`, `LatticeExhaustion`), `AlphaData` exposes exactly two premises as explicit fields, plus one convention:\n\n* `symplectic` — the coordinate map preserves the symplectic form (the antisymmetrisations of the source and target Pauli pairings agree). Needed for symmetry of the discrepancy matrix, without which no phase calibration exists at all.\n* `stage_surjective` — at each stage the coordinate map is *onto* the regional labels. P52 gives injectivity and `⊆` only; this is the finite-stage form of the manuscript's \"hyperbolic pairs are a basis of V_Γ\" clause.\n* `[LinearOrder I]` — a linear order on the coordinate index, used only to fix the ordering convention of the quadratic phase refinement (data, not a restriction).\n\nTo rule out vacuity, `standardAlphaData` exhibits a witness satisfying both premises: the tautological hyperbolic coordinates on the