itions used consistently throughout the derivation?\n- Is any implication actually reversible, or was a one-way statement used both\n  ways?\n- Are there division-by-zero, invertibility, regularity, convergence, branch-cut,\n  gauge, or boundary-term assumptions?\n- Do limiting cases, dimensions/units, symmetries, and known special cases agree?\n- Are symbolic substitutions justified rather than smuggling in the result?\n- Are claims labeled correctly as proof, derivation, check, conjecture, or\n  numerical evidence?\n\n## TeX And Source-Backed Checks\n\n- Does the document compile if compilation was expected?\n- Are labels, references, citations, bibliography entries, and figure paths valid?\n- Are source-backed claims tied to exact locators when required?\n- Is quoted or paraphrased material clearly separated from the agent's synthesis?\n- Does the exposition define terms before using them in load-bearing statements?\n\n## Computation Checks\n\n- Is the computation reproducible from a recorded command?\n- Are inputs, random seeds, versions, tolerances, and units documented when they\n  affect the result?\n- Are outputs interpreted correctly and not over-promoted beyond the computation?\n- Were independent sanity checks used where feasible: small cases, limiting\n  cases, dimensional analysis, symbolic identities, or alternate algorithms?\n\n## Closeout Template\n\nUse this structure internally, then surface the concise version to the user:\n\n```text\nFindings:\n- [severity] file/path:line - issue and consequence.\n\nChecks run:\n- command -> result.\n\nResidual risk:\n- what was not checked, or why the artifact is not a proof/complete validation.\n\nCleanup:\n- remaining dirty/untracked files and whether they are intentional.\n```\n--- TARGETED SEMANTIC AUDIT EVIDENCE ---\n7-# P53 — the algebraic `alpha` of the local-hyperbolic coordinates\n8-\n9-Context declaration: **source basis** `main.tex:1898-1944` (the proposed\n10:`∗`-isomorphism `α : 𝒫_I → 𝒜_Γ` determined on the adapted symplectic basis by\n11-`α(X_i) = P(x_i)`, `α(Z_i) = P(z_i)` and \"extended to a homomorphism\"), read\n12:together with `main.tex:1671-1679` (short-range order: a symplectic basis of\n13-hyperbolic pairs, each locally supported).\n14-\n15-This module instantiates the checked cocycle/word-basis/coherence/direct-limit\n--\n50-* `linearOrder`: a linear order on the coordinate index type `I`, used only to\n51-  fix the ordering convention of the quadratic phase refinement.  (Every set\n52-  admits one; it is data, not a restriction.)\n53:* `symplectic`: the coordinate map preserves the symplectic form, i.e. the\n54-  antisymmetrisations of the source and target Pauli cocycles agree.  This is\n55:  the content of the manuscript's word *symplectic* basis; without it no phase\n56-  calibration whatsoever exists, since the two multiplier cocycles then differ\n57-  by a non-symmetric class.\n58:* `stage_surjective`: at every stage the coordinate map carries the stage-`n`\n59-  source labels **onto** the stage-`n` target labels.  P52 proves injectivity\n60-  and `⊆`; surjectivity is the finite-stage form of the manuscript's clause\n61-  that the hyperbolic pairs are a *basis* of `V_Γ` with `|I| = |Γ|`, and it is\n--\n72-\n73-## What is *not* claimed\n74-\n75:Everything below is algebra.  No C⋆-norm, completion, state identity, GNS\n76:representation, tensor factorization, factorhood, trace or weight statement is\n77-used or claimed.\n78--/\n79-\n--\n452-\n453-/-- **The data of this packet.**  On top of the P52 local-hyperbolic family and\n454-lattice exhaustion it carries exactly two auxiliary assumptions: the coordinate\n455:map is symplectic, and it is onto the finite target labels at every stage. -/\n456-structure AlphaData (L I : Type*) [LinearOrder I] where\n457-  /-- The P52 locally supported adapted hyperbolic family. -/\n458-  family : CoherentLocalHyperbolic.LocalHyperbolicFamily L I\n459-  /-- The P52 lattice exhaustion. -/\n460-  exhaustion : CoherentLocalHyperbolic.LatticeExhaustion L\n461:  /-- **Auxiliary assumption (symplectic coordinates).**  The coordinate map\n462:  preserves the symplectic form, i.e. the antisymmetrisations of the source and\n463-  target Pauli pairings agree. -/\n464:  symplectic : ∀ v w : PauliCoordinateLabels I,\n465-    (coordPairing I).form v w + (coordPairing I).form w v =\n466-      (coordPairing L).form (family.coordinateMap v) (family.coordinateMap w) +\n467-        (coordPairing L).form (family.coordinateMap w) (family.coordinateMap v)\n468-  /-- **Auxiliary assumption (finite-stage adaptedness).**  At every stage the\n469-  coordinate map is onto the stage labels of the region. -/\n470:  stage_surjective : ∀ (n : ℕ), ∀ u ∈ exhaustion.targetLabels n,\n471-    ∃ c ∈ family.sourceLabels exhaustion n, family.coordinateMap c = u\n472-\n473-namespace AlphaData\n--\n518-    ((A.stageLabelMap n v : A.TargetLabel n) : CoherentLocalHyperbolic.PhaseSpace L) =\n519-      A.family.coordinateMap (v : PauliCoordinateLabels I) := rfl\n520-\n521:theorem stageLabelMap_bijective (n : ℕ) : Function.Bijective (A.stageLabelMap n) := by\n522-  constructor\n523-  · intro v w h\n524-    exact A.family.blockCoordinateMap_injective A.exhaustion n h\n525-  · intro u\n526:    obtain ⟨c, hc, hcu⟩ := A.stage_surjective n (u : CoherentLocalHyperbolic.PhaseSpace L) u.2\n527-    exact ⟨⟨c, hc⟩, Subtype.ext hcu⟩\n528-\n529-/-- The stage-`n` label bijection. -/\n530-noncomputable def stageLabelEquiv (n : ℕ) : A.SourceLabel n ≃ A.TargetLabel n :=\n531:  Equiv.ofBijective _ (A.stageLabelMap_bijective n)\n532-\n533-\n534-/-! ### The phase calibration -/\n--\n560-  fun p q => A.discForm.form (Finsupp.single p 1) (Finsupp.single q 1)\n561-\n562-theorem discrepancy_symm (p q : I ⊕ I) : A.discrepancy p q = A.discrepancy q p := by\n563:  exact pauliBit_cross (A.symplectic (Finsupp.single p 1) (Finsupp.single q 1))\n564-\n565-theorem coordinateBilinear_discrepancy (v w : PauliCoordinateLabels I) :\n566-    coordinate